{
 "about": "Normalizer of the sketch world. Deterministic rules applied before the VSS reader, identically in Python (normalize.py, used by the generator) and in JavaScript (docs/js/snorm.js, used by the demo). Order: quoted strings become one TEXT token (t_...); lower-case; contractions; punctuation split; leading politeness removed; sentence-initial rewrites (question openers become pseudo-verbs); multi-word expressions, longest first; single-word synonyms; number words to digits ('one' never); finally every token that is not in the lexicon, not a number and not punctuation becomes a NAME token (n_...). The reader never sees the surface forms on the left. A capital 'A' is the article only when the next word is one of article_followers; otherwise it is the shape named A. A capital 'A' right after one of name_before is always the name. 'the new / last / latest' become the determiner token newest, 'the first / oldest' the token oldest. Rewrites (after names): when the first token is one of `first` and, for each list in `all`, one of its words occurs, the first token becomes `set` (the question forms of extreme, nearest, connected and degree). A word outside the lexicon becomes a NAME token only when it is a known shape name, is capitalised and not the message's first word, or is the capital A in a name position; any other unknown word stays as it is (the reader's kind 'unknown': placed, never a filler). After a question verb, a later 'is' / 'are' becomes 'be' (an auxiliary, not the fact verb).",
 "contractions": {
  "don't": "do not",
  "dont": "do not",
  "let's": "lets",
  "can't": "can not",
